  "title": "Exact Sprague–Grundy Words for the Three-Move Subtraction Games {2,5,c}",
  "batch_label": "67",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer c>5 with c!=7, Conjecture 50 of arXiv:2609.05358v1 holds for the subtraction game S={2,5,c}. More precisely, the source-proved residues 1,2,3,5,6 modulo 7 are purely periodic. In the two remaining residues the exact Sprague-Grundy words and minimal parameters are: for every K>=1, g_{7K+4}=(0011021)^K 0011223 (021021 (0011021)^K)^infinity with (q,p)=(7K+7,7K+6)=(c+3,c+2); and for every K>=2, g_{7K}=(0011021)^K 32203103 (1 (0011021)^(K-1) 02102102)^infinity with (q,p)=(7K+8,7K+2)=(c+8,c+2). Thus both uncovered residue classes have positive minimal preperiod, completing the conjecture on the entire frozen shape.",
